    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI don't think having a dedicated mapping for it is needed. Especially I'd suggest to not use `p` as it is a \"paste\" key that can be used during text editing in 'mini.files' buffers.\n\nTake a look at #936, in particular [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/936#discussioncomment-11178002). To go even further, you can follow [this example]() and do something like this:\n\n```lua\nlocal toggle_preview = function()\n  MiniFiles.config.windows.preview = not MiniFiles.config.windows.preview\n  MiniFiles.refresh({})\nend\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\n  callback = function(args)\n    local buf_id = args.data.buf_id\n    -- Tweak left-hand side of mapping to your liking\n    vim.keymap.set('n', 'gp', toggle_preview, { buffer = buf_id })\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nThis will have \"global\" effect, i.e. preview will be toggled not only for current but for all next explorers. And yes, it does require manual cursor movement to take full effect.\n\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2025-01-23T09:01:41Z",
